## 14. 📋 Definition of Done Checklist

Work through this list in order before calling M2 complete.

### 🗄️ Database

- [ ] Alembic revision `002_scraper_full` runs cleanly from `migrate` container
- [ ] `programs`, `program_scopes`, `program_policies` tables exist with correct columns
- [ ] `alembic current` shows revision `002`
- [ ] All indexes created: `ix_programs_platform`, `ix_programs_queued_for_scan`, `ix_program_scopes_program_id`
- [ ] Downgrade path (`002` → `001`) tested and verified

### 🧩 Collector Abstraction

- [ ] `BaseCollector` abstract class with `fetch_listing`, `fetch_details`, `normalize` defined
- [ ] `CollectorRegistry` maps `"hackerone"` → `HackerOneCollector`
- [ ] `@register("hackerone")` decorator applied to `HackerOneCollector`
- [ ] `get_collector("unknown_platform")` raises `CollectorError`

### 🕵️ HackerOne Collector

- [ ] `_get_with_retry` handles `429` with `Retry-After` delay
- [ ] `_get_with_retry` raises `CollectorAuthError` on `401`/`403` without retrying
- [ ] `_get_with_retry` raises `CollectorRateLimitError` after max retries exhausted
- [ ] `fetch_listing` skips programs that fail `fetch_details` (does not abort the full run)
- [ ] `fetch_details` uses `/structured_scopes` endpoint — NOT raw policy text
- [ ] `H1_ASSET_TYPE_MAP` covers all known HackerOne `asset_type` values
- [ ] `normalize` produces a dict that maps directly to `programs` table columns

### 🔭 Scope Parser

- [ ] Wildcard: `*.example.com` and `.example.com` both normalise to `*.example.com`
- [ ] CIDR: `/32` normalises to host address; `/24` preserved as-is
- [ ] URL: trailing slash stripped
- [ ] Domain: lowercased, trailing dot removed
- [ ] Empty `value` entries filtered out (not an error)
- [ ] Unrecognised `asset_type` falls back to value-based inference
- [ ] `out_of_scope` scope_type preserved correctly

### 🗃️ Repository & Upsert

- [ ] `upsert` on a new program: row created in `programs`, scopes in `program_scopes`
- [ ] `upsert` on an existing program: fields updated, `queued_for_scan` **NOT** overwritten
- [ ] `upsert` replaces scopes on every call (delete + re-insert)
- [ ] `upsert` creates/updates policy in `program_policies`
- [ ] `set_queued_for_scan` sets the flag correctly in both directions
- [ ] `get_programs_pending_reconcile` only returns programs within the stale window

### 📤 Queue Publisher

- [ ] `ScanJobPublisher.publish_scan_job` builds a valid `ScanJobsPayload`
- [ ] Successful publish sets `queued_for_scan = false`
- [ ] Failed publish sets `queued_for_scan = true`
- [ ] Programs with no in-scope entries are skipped (not published, not flagged)

### ♻️ Reconciler

- [ ] Reconciler queries `queued_for_scan = true AND last_scraped_at > NOW() - N days`
- [ ] Successful republish: `queued_for_scan` cleared
